# Failure Recovery Builder Skill

Use this skill when the user asks to add failure recovery, build kill switches, or set up the apocalypse fallback.

## The principle

**June's offer-design rule (per memory):** plan for tech failures. Every visible action on stage must have a backup that the audience cannot distinguish from the live version.

The pattern: **live → fake → safe**, three layers deep. Live is real APIs. Fake is pre-rendered MP4s queued and instant. Safe is a static screenshot with no animation.

If everything is broken (no internet, dead laptop), the apocalypse fallback is a USB stick with Chrome + static HTML that runs entirely offline.

## Mode pattern (every sub-tool implements this)

```tsx
// src/components/tools/cmo/InstagramCreator.tsx
"use client";
import { useSelector } from "@xstate/react";
import { stageActor } from "@/lib/machine";

export function InstagramCreator() {
  const mode = useSelector(stageActor, (s) => s.context.mode);

  // SAFE: instant fallback (no animation, just last frame)
  if (mode === "safe") {
    return (
      <div className="fixed inset-0 bg-black flex items-center justify-center">
        <img src="/safe/cmo-instagram-still.png" className="w-full h-full object-contain" />
      </div>
    );
  }

  // FAKE: pre-rendered MP4 plays instantly
  if (mode === "fake") {
    return (
      <video
        src="/fallback/cmo-instagram.mp4"
        autoPlay
        className="fixed inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
    );
  }

  // LIVE: real API call to Anthropic + fal.ai
  return <LiveInstagramCreator />;
}
```

