## The apocalypse fallback (USB stick)

Build a fully-static fallback that runs from a USB stick if WiFi dies AND backup laptop fails:

```bash
# Build process (run on Day 6)
cd gbi-2026/
npm run build  # static export to out/

# Copy a portable Chrome to the USB stick
# Mac: download "Chrome portable" or use system Chrome
# Copy out/ folder to USB

# Launch script for USB stick:
cat > /Volumes/USB/run-stage.sh <<'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
open -a "Google Chrome" --args --kiosk --app="file:///Volumes/USB/out/index.html"
EOF
chmod +x /Volumes/USB/run-stage.sh
```

When run from USB, the demo plays exclusively from cached MP4s and static content. Zero internet required. Audience sees a 90% identical demo (no real LLM streams, but all 14 fallback MP4s play). They cannot tell the difference.

